---
/* Flight Plan deep page, Pre-flight / Liftoff / Orbit from 2026.09.10 dump.
   Linked from homepage system section, nav, and footer.
   Layout follows Claude Design "The Flight Plan.dc.html": hero with a stack of
   tilted photo cards, then each stage as an orange-railed copy column beside a
   single photo card, ending on the dark CTA panel. Copy is ours, not the mock's.
   Photos go through <Picture> (see src/data/images.js) like the rest of the site. */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Picture from '../components/Picture.astro';
import { absoluteUrl, breadcrumbList, graph, webPageNode } from '../data/schema';

const title = 'Flight Plan to Scale Home Service Shops | Local Service Rocket';
const description =
  'Pre-flight builds the structure: site, GBP, LSA, lead profiles. Liftoff is when organic and LSA compound and Search is ready. Orbit scales ads, hiring, pricing, and process.';
const pageUrl = absoluteUrl('/flight-plan/');
const jsonLd = graph([
  webPageNode({ pageUrl, name: title, description }),
  breadcrumbList(pageUrl, [
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Flight Plan', path: '/flight-plan' },
  ]),
]);

// Hero cards render at 195px, stage cards at 260px.
const HERO_CARD_SIZES = '(max-width: 900px) 40vw, 195px';
const STAGE_CARD_SIZES = '(max-width: 900px) 90vw, 260px';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <main class="container">
    <div class="crumbs">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <span class="current">The Flight Plan</span>
    </div>

    <!-- HERO -->
    <div class="hero">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <div class="eyebrow">THE FLIGHT PLAN</div>
        <h1>Flight Plan From One-Man Shop to Real Company</h1>
        <p>
          Most owners we help start around <strong>$20-25k/month</strong> and want consistent leads,
          a small crew, or a path toward roughly <strong>$2-3M/year</strong>. The path is the same
          either way: build the structure, watch it start working, then scale ads, hiring, pricing,
          and process. You always know where you are and what’s next.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-ctas">
          <a href="/get-started" class="btn btn-primary">Schedule onboarding</a>
          <a href="/case-studies" class="btn btn-secondary">See client results</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="photo-stack">
        <figure class="photo-card card-a">
          <Picture
            name="team-honest-hanks"
            alt="The Honest Hank's crew"
            sizes={HERO_CARD_SIZES}
            loading="eager"
            fetchpriority="high"
            style="object-position: center 60%"
          />
          <figcaption>Honest Hank’s · Tampa, FL</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="photo-card card-b">
          <Picture name="team-dry-duck" alt="The Dry Duck crew" sizes={HERO_CARD_SIZES} />
          <figcaption>Dry Duck · Iowa</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="photo-card card-c">
          <Picture name="team-rewired" alt="The Rewired crew" sizes={HERO_CARD_SIZES} />
          <figcaption>Rewired · Des Moines, IA</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- STAGE 1 -->
    <section class="stage" id="pre-flight">
      <div class="stage-copy">
        <div class="stage-label">STAGE 1</div>
        <h2>Pre-flight: build the structure</h2>
        <p class="stage-lede">
          We work with you to build the website, Google Business Profile, Local Services Ads setup,
          and lead profiles so you start getting consistent leads. This stage is about building the
          structure, not pouring money into Search yet.
        </p>
        <div class="example">
          <div class="example-tag">EXAMPLE · HONEST HANK’S</div>
          <p>
            Lewis was a serious one-man / rag-tag shop at roughly <strong>$20-25k/month</strong> who
            wanted consistent leads and a real company (even if that meant stopping at a few employees).
            First moves: audit where leads actually came from, tighten the Google Business Profile and
            website, citations / chamber / BBB-style foundations, Local Services Ads, and platforms like
            Angi and Yelp for reviews and links, even when they’re inefficient lead sources, until his
            own Google system could carry the load.
          </p>
          <p>
            Ready for Liftoff looked like: booked jobs climbing toward that daily rhythm and revenue
            around <strong>$25k/month</strong>, enough to think about vans and hiring.
          </p>
          <a href="/case-studies/honest-hanks">Read the Honest Hank’s story →</a>
        </div>
        <ul class="bullets">
          <li>Website that converts (build or rebuild if needed)</li>
          <li>Google Business Profile optimized for the words homeowners type</li>
          <li>Local Services Ads set up and producing booked calls</li>
          <li>Lead profiles and foundations so volume is consistent, not accidental</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="stage-photo">
        <figure class="photo-card tilt-right">
          <Picture
            name="team-honest-hanks"
            alt="The Honest Hank's crew"
            sizes={STAGE_CARD_SIZES}
            style="object-position: center 60%"
          />
          <figcaption>Honest Hank's: one man to three techs</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- STAGE 2 -->
    <section class="stage" id="liftoff">
      <div class="stage-copy">
        <div class="stage-label">STAGE 2</div>
        <h2>Liftoff: the structure starts working</h2>
        <p class="stage-lede">
          Liftoff is when the structure we built begins to rank on Google. The website brings in leads
          for free, the GBP does too, LSA lead flow is climbing, and Google Search Ads are ready to
          start on a small budget.
        </p>
        <div class="example">
          <div class="example-tag">WHAT SCALES HERE</div>
          <p>
            Stronger SEO frameworks (area posts, GBP reach, selective backlinks). Branding by Liftoff
            at latest, Honest Hank’s did it early in Pre-flight, which is fine if cash allows ($5k
            <a href="/services/branding">brand package</a>). Then Search/PPC on a small daily budget once
            SEO foundations exist, so paid isn’t fighting a broken site.
          </p>
          <p>
            Our fee around this stage: <strong>~$1.5k/mo</strong> covering SEO and ad management
            together, plus LSA on a pay-per-booked-call model. Still in the ~10-15% of revenue
            ballpark once ad spend is included.
          </p>
        </div>
        <ul class="bullets">
          <li>Organic rankings compound: free leads from the site and map pack</li>
          <li>GBP and LSA volume climb as relevance and reviews stack</li>
          <li>Google Search Ads ready to start (~$50/day tests)</li>
          <li>Brand system homeowners trust (logo, trucks, uniforms)</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="stage-photo">
        <figure class="photo-card tilt-left">
          <Picture name="team-dry-duck" alt="The Dry Duck crew" sizes={STAGE_CARD_SIZES} />
          <figcaption>Dry Duck: brand, site and wraps built from scratch</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- STAGE 3 -->
    <section class="stage" id="orbit">
      <div class="stage-copy">
        <div class="stage-label">STAGE 3</div>
        <h2>Orbit: scale, hire, improve</h2>
        <p class="stage-lede">
          Orbit is about scaling ads further, supporting hiring, raising sales pricing, and
          improving processes so the company isn’t you in every truck.
        </p>
        <div class="example">
          <div class="example-tag">EXAMPLE · HONEST HANK’S HIRING</div>
          <p>
            After burning ~$1k+ on Indeed with nothing to show, we ran Facebook hiring. Within ~10 days
            they had candidates interviewing. Full transparency: they ultimately hired via
            friends/referrals, but the sprint still produced a real pipeline fast. Owner job: define
            the role and take interviews. Our job: ads + filters. Their ongoing job: train new hires to
            produce, we support, we don’t pretend to run their shop.
          </p>
          <p>
            Rewired and Dry Duck live in this world too: scaled crews, higher ad risk, and fees that
            reflect insurance against a working system failing when you’re at $200k months with trucks
            and payroll to feed.
          </p>
          <a href="/services/hiring">See hiring &amp; recruiting →</a>
        </div>
        <ul class="bullets">
          <li>Scale Search carefully: ~$1.5k/mo + 20% of ad spend covers risk as budgets rise</li>
          <li>Hiring support (~$500 setup / ~$500 month while live) when trucks are the bottleneck</li>
          <li>Raise sales pricing and tighten processes as volume and crew grow</li>
          <li>Owner becomes the trainer/operator; we keep Google printing</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="stage-photo">
        <figure class="photo-card tilt-right">
          <Picture name="team-rewired" alt="The Rewired crew" sizes={STAGE_CARD_SIZES} />
          <figcaption>Rewired: five techs to twelve</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="sweet">
      <h2>Where Electrical and Trade Shops Fit</h2>
      <p>
        We’re built for roughly <strong>$20-25k/month → ~$200k/month</strong> on Google, the climb
        to about <strong>$2-3M/year</strong>. Past that, some shops outgrow a focused Google partner
        and want a larger in-house or multi-channel team. That’s fine. Our job is to get you to the
        point where those options exist.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="cta-panel">
      <div>
        <div class="cta-title">Know which stage you’re in?</div>
        <p>Watch how it works, then book onboarding. No sales calls.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cta-actions">
        <a href="/get-started" class="btn btn-primary">Schedule onboarding</a>
        <a href="/case-studies" class="btn btn-ghost-dark">See client results</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  main {
    padding-top: 40px;
    padding-bottom: 72px;
  }

  .crumbs {
    display: flex;
    gap: 10px;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--muted-3);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .crumbs a {
    color: var(--muted-3);
  }

  .current {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* HERO */
  .hero {
    margin-top: 24px;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 440px;
    gap: 48px;
    align-items: center;
  }

  h1 {
    margin-top: 12px;
    font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 44px);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    line-height: 1.1;
    text-wrap: balance;
    max-width: 18ch;
  }

  .hero-copy > p {
    margin-top: 16px;
    font-size: 16.5px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--muted);
    max-width: 52ch;
  }

  .hero-ctas {
    display: flex;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-top: 24px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  /* Tilted photo cards, shared by the hero stack and the stage sidebars. */
  .photo-card {
    margin: 0;
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 8px 8px 10px;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 22px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12);
  }

  /* :global() because <Picture> renders the <img> from a child component. */
  .photo-card :global(img) {
    width: 100%;
    height: 115px;
    object-fit: cover;
    border-radius: 3px;
    display: block;
  }

  .photo-card figcaption {
    margin-top: 7px;
    font-size: 10.5px;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--body);
  }

  .photo-stack {
    position: relative;
    height: 320px;
  }

  .photo-stack .photo-card {
    position: absolute;
    width: 195px;
  }

  .card-a {
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    transform: rotate(-5deg);
  }

  .card-b {
    top: 58px;
    right: 0;
    transform: rotate(4deg);
  }

  .card-c {
    bottom: 0;
    left: 40px;
    transform: rotate(-2deg);
  }

  /* STAGES */
  .stage {
    margin-top: 64px;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 260px;
    gap: 40px;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .stage-copy {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--orange);
    padding-left: 28px;
  }

  .stage-label {
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--orange);
  }

  .stage h2 {
    margin-top: 8px;
    font-size: 28px;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .stage-lede {
    margin-top: 12px;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--body);
    font-weight: 600;
    max-width: 68ch;
  }

  .stage-photo :global(img) {
    height: 150px;
  }

  .tilt-right {
    transform: rotate(3deg);
  }

  .tilt-left {
    transform: rotate(-3deg);
  }

  .example {
    margin-top: 22px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-panel);
    padding: 22px 26px;
    background: var(--section-bg);
  }

  .example-tag {
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.07em;
    color: var(--orange);
  }

  .example p {
    margin-top: 10px;
    font-size: 14.5px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--body);
    max-width: 78ch;
  }

  .example a {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 12px;
    font-size: 13.5px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--orange);
  }

  .bullets {
    margin: 18px 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--body);
  }

  .bullets li {
    padding-left: 20px;
    position: relative;
  }

  .bullets li::before {
    content: '·';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--orange);
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  /* WHERE WE FIT */
  .sweet {
    margin-top: 64px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--section-bg);
    border-radius: var(--radius-panel);
    padding: 32px 36px;
  }

  .sweet h2 {
    font-size: 24px;
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .sweet p {
    margin-top: 10px;
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--body);
    max-width: 72ch;
  }

  /* CTA */
  .cta-panel {
    margin-top: 56px;
    background: var(--dark);
    color: var(--dark-text);
    border-radius: 20px;
    padding: 36px 40px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 30px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .cta-title {
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .cta-panel p {
    margin: 6px 0 0;
    font-size: 13.5px;
    color: var(--dark-muted);
  }

  .cta-actions {
    display: flex;
    gap: 12px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  @media (max-width: 1000px) {
    .hero {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 36px;
    }

    /* Overlapping cards need room they do not have on narrow screens. */
    .photo-stack {
      height: auto;
      display: flex;
      gap: 12px;
      justify-content: center;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }

    .photo-stack .photo-card {
      position: static;
      width: min(195px, 30vw);
    }

    .photo-stack :global(img) {
      height: 90px;
    }

    .stage {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 28px;
    }

    .stage-photo {
      order: -1;
      max-width: 340px;
    }

    .stage-photo :global(img) {
      height: 170px;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .stage-copy {
      padding-left: 18px;
    }

    .example {
      padding: 20px 18px;
    }

    .cta-panel {
      padding: 28px 22px;
    }
  }
</style>
